    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26353" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Leucas</span></b> , ădis,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λευκάς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> For Leucadia, v. h.
			v.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The capital of the island Leucadia;</i> v.
			Leucadia, B.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The promontory Leucata;</i> v.
			Leucata.</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> †
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leucaspis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj., f.</i>, =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεύκασπις</span>, <i>armed with a white shield</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">phalanx,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 41</span></i>
			.</div>
